Create one image for a CoCo 3 game. The whole image will be reduced to a 48x40 grid of target pixels (gime-320x16). On the display, each target pixel is 0.857:1, width to height.
Use only these 16 colours, each as flat areas: black $00 (#141414), dark grey $10 (#3F3F3F), grey $20 (#9A9A9A), white $30 (#FFFFFF), brown $05 (#751D02), orange $15 (#E75D1F), tan $25 (#FFB053), yellow $24 (#FFC82E), dark green $0E (#004315), green $12 (#47910B), light green $21 (#63FF30), blue $0B (#221CDE), sky blue $1C (#227FF1), cyan $2D (#43F8FF), dark red $07 (#9B123C), red $16 (#FF4F4B). Do not use gradients, dithering, anti-aliasing, texture or any other colour.
Make every important shape at least 3 target pixels across: at least 6.2% of the image width and 7.5% of the image height. Leave out detail smaller than that.
Follow the JSON specification below exactly. The Context section explains why the image exists. Do not draw anything from it. Do not draw text, letters or numbers unless the specification explicitly asks for them.
The background must be fully transparent. Give the subject crisp, hard edges, with no semi-transparent glow, shadow or fringe, and leave generous padding around the subject.

The reference images are given in this order:
1. An approved style sample. Match its style (the owner-approved style for every creature: thick black outline, flat colour with one darker shade step, big white eyes with black pupils, chibi proportions, cheerful open-mouth smile, the same scale and padding), but use only the listed colours.
Take the pose, view and composition from the specification, not from the reference images.

